{
  "member": "mcp",
  "model": "models/ConnectionTable.tla",
  "scope": "finite models: ConnectionTable (the connection table of Streamable HTTP endpoints with a credential: one or two keys, at most two ensure, one release, one closeAll, one lose, one port deviation; bounds fire in creation order; two keys fire no bound), Calls (the call port over an abstract table: at most four keys, one correlation key, one task), Continuation (one action call as a checkpointed entry source: at most three checkpoints, one task, two process losses) and Events (one event subscription: three events, two subscribers, two process losses). Safety, and P8 T1 and P14 T1 under weak fairness. No refinement proof between the models or to the implementation; no real transport, peer or storage.",
